  "attestation": 1.25,
  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 2025, a Pentagon office set up to look into unexplained aerial sightings, known as AARO, is said to have told the Wall Street Journal reporter Joel Schectman that a shutdown of nuclear missiles had been some kind of EMP test. An EMP is an electromagnetic pulse, a burst of energy that can knock out electronics. The story comes from Robert Salas, a former Air Force officer who says he was there when the missiles went down, and he tells it to explain where the newspaper's account of that shutdown came from."
}
